# 3. ARCHITECTURE

Single Gradle module, package-by-feature, with a hard dependency direction: `ui → domain → data`. `domain` has **zero Android imports** (no `Context`, no `android.*`) so every game rule is unit-testable on the JVM.

```
app/src/main/java/com/nawawia/
├─ NawawiaApp.kt            // Application, owns AppContainer
├─ AppContainer.kt          // manual DI: repositories, player, clock
├─ core/
│  ├─ clock/AppClock.kt     // interface { fun now(): Instant; fun zone(): ZoneId } — NEVER call Instant.now() directly
│  ├─ result/AppResult.kt   // sealed Success/Failure(AppError). No exceptions across layer boundaries.
│  └─ error/AppError.kt     // sealed: ContentMissing, ContentCorrupt, AudioUnavailable, StorageFailure, LinkBlocked
├─ data/
│  ├─ content/              // ContentLoader, integrity verification, DTOs
│  ├─ db/                   // Room: entities, DAOs, migrations (Migration_1_2 etc. — written from day one)
│  ├─ prefs/                // DataStore settings
│  └─ audio/                // AudioManifest, AudioRepository, Media3 wrapper
├─ domain/                  // PURE KOTLIN — no android.* imports, enforced by a lint rule
│  ├─ model/                // Hadith, Unit, Question, Attempt, Mastery, Streak, Hearts
│  ├─ game/                 // HeartsEngine, XpEngine, StreakEngine, ScoringEngine
│  ├─ srs/                  // Sm2Scheduler
│  └─ usecase/
├─ ui/
│  ├─ theme/                // tokens, color schemes, type, shape, motion — §5
│  ├─ components/           // ChunkyButton, PathNode, HeartBar, StreakFlame, MatnCard, AnswerChoice, StateBox...
│  └─ feature/              // onboarding, path, hadith, lesson, result, review, profile, settings
└─ res/
   ├─ values/strings.xml    // ar (default locale)
   ├─ values-en/strings.xml
   └─ font/                 // bundled OFL fonts — no runtime font download
```

**State:** one `UiState` data class per screen, exposed as `StateFlow` from a `ViewModel`; events in as a sealed `Intent`. Composables receive state + a lambda, nothing else. **No business logic inside a `@Composable`.** No `GlobalScope`; all coroutines in `viewModelScope` or a scoped `CoroutineScope` owned by `AppContainer`.

**`AppClock` is mandatory.** Streaks, hearts refill and SRS intervals all read time through it. Tests inject a `FakeClock`. Any direct `System.currentTimeMillis()`, `Instant.now()`, `LocalDate.now()` or `Calendar.getInstance()` outside `AppClock` is a build-blocking defect.

