# 7. GAME SYSTEMS — exact formulas, all pure functions, all unit-tested

### 7.1 Hearts
Max 5. −1 per wrong answer. Refill: **one heart per 30 minutes**, computed from `lastHeartSpentAt` on read — `heartsNow = min(5, stored + floor(minutesSince / 30))`, then persist the recomputed value and advance the anchor. **No timers, no services, no `WorkManager`** for this. It must be correct after a 3-day app kill. A completed review set grants +1 heart (capped at 5).

### 7.2 XP
`xp = 10 × correctFirstTry + 2 × correctAfterRetry + unitBonus(50) + dailyGoalBonus(20) + streakMultiplier`, where `streakMultiplier = min(streakDays / 7, 2) × 5`, integer-floored. Document it in `DECISIONS.md`; the numbers are yours to keep but the formula must be a single pure function with tests.

### 7.3 Streak — the single most bug-prone system. Specify and test it this way.
- Store `lastActiveEpochDay: Long` (epoch days **in the user's current zone**, via `AppClock`) and `streakDays: Int`, plus `freezesAvailable: Int` (max 2, one earned per 7-day streak).
- On completing any lesson: `today = LocalDate.now(clock.zone()).toEpochDay()`.
  - `today == last` → no change.
  - `today == last + 1` → `streakDays++`.
  - `today > last + 1` → if `freezesAvailable > 0 && today == last + 2` consume one freeze and `streakDays++`; else `streakDays = 1`.
  - **`today < last`** → the clock moved backwards (timezone change, manual clock change, DST). **Do not increment, do not reset, do not reward.** Keep `streakDays`, keep `last` at the max of the two, and record one local diagnostic counter. This is the anti-cheat and anti-DST branch, and it is the one AI-written streaks always get wrong.
- Required test matrix (write every one): same day · next day · 2-day gap with freeze · 2-day gap without freeze · 5-day gap · DST forward · DST backward · travel UTC+3→UTC−5 · travel UTC−5→UTC+3 · device clock set back one day · device clock set forward one year · year boundary · leap day · first-ever lesson.

### 7.4 Mastery & SRS (SM-2)
Per hadith: `easeFactor` (start 2.5, floor 1.3), `intervalDays`, `repetitions`, `dueEpochDay`, `masteryPct (0..100)`. Grade from the lesson: all first-try correct → 5; one retry → 4; two → 3; hearts exhausted → 2. `Sm2Scheduler` is a pure function `(state, grade) -> state` with tests for grades 0–5, first review, lapse, and ease-factor floor. `masteryPct` is derived from `repetitions` and last grade — never a random number, never a UI-only value.

### 7.5 Achievements
Pure predicates over stored stats, evaluated on write, never recomputed in the UI: أول حديث · أول وحدة · ٧ أيام · ٣٠ يومًا · ١٠٠ يوم · مراجعة كاملة في ١٠ دقائق · ٤٢/٤٢ · ١٠٠٠ XP. Each has a locked and an unlocked state with a `contentDescription`.

