# 9. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA — the gap list

Each item is a pass/fail check. The Stage 7 report answers every one with file:line or a test name. These are the specific ways AI-generated Android apps fail; closing them is the point of this document.

**Content & correctness**
1. No hadith text, takhrīj, grading, translation, question, option or distractor anywhere in the repo was written by you.
2. Content integrity gate implemented with all 7 checks and 7 failing-fixture tests; failure blocks the app with no fallback.
3. 42 hadith asserted; `number` is exactly 1..42, no gaps or duplicates.
4. No hadith renders without its takhrīj line.
5. Matn is never trimmed, normalized, truncated or ellipsized; tashkeel renders intact at every text size.
6. Copy/share of matn always carries the takhrīj.

**Security & privacy**
7. Manifest declares only `INTERNET`, `POST_NOTIFICATIONS`, `RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED`. No storage, location, contacts, camera, mic, phone-state, `QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES`.
8. No API keys, tokens or secrets in the repo or the APK. No `.env`, no keystore, no `google-services.json` committed; `.gitignore` covers them.
9. No analytics, ads, attribution or crash SDK. Data Safety answer is "no data collected, no data shared" — and it is true.
10. `LinkGuard` allowlist is exact-host-or-subdomain; a `dorar.net.evil.com` test case is blocked by a unit test.
11. `android:allowBackup` decision is explicit and justified; `android:exported` is explicit on every component; no implicitly exported receiver.
12. Export / import / delete-my-data all work; delete actually clears Room **and** DataStore **and** cached files.

**State & data**
13. All time flows through `AppClock`; zero direct `now()` calls outside it (verified by a repo-wide search in the report).
14. Full streak matrix of §7.3 passes, including clock-rollback and both travel directions.
15. Hearts are correct after a 3-day process kill, with no timer or service.
16. Room migrations exist from v1; `fallbackToDestructiveMigration` appears nowhere.
17. Progress is written after every answer in a transaction; killing the app mid-lesson loses nothing.
18. Seeded shuffle: rotation and process death restore identical question order.
19. Every repository IO returns `AppResult`; no `catch (e: Exception) {}`, no `!!`, no `lateinit` that can be read before init, no `GlobalScope`.

**Android platform**
20. `compileSdk`/`targetSdk` 36, `minSdk` 24, builds with no warnings-as-errors suppressions.
21. Edge-to-edge on every screen with correct status/nav/cutout/IME insets; nothing tappable under system bars; lists have bottom content padding clearing the nav bar and the floating CTA.
22. Predictive back works everywhere; back from a lesson confirms before discarding; back never traps.
23. Rotation, dark-mode toggle, font-scale change and display-size change lose no state on any screen.
24. **RTL audit:** zero `paddingLeft/Right`/`alignLeft` — `start`/`end` only; directional icons use `autoMirrored`; progress bars fill right-to-left; swipes mirrored; the week grid starts on the right. Verified with `adb shell settings put global debug.force_rtl 1` **and** in Arabic locale.
